      "residue_after": "G",
      "residue_label": "K155",
      "topology_state": "O",
      "extracellular": true,
      "compartment": "extracellular",
      "tag_type": "HA",
      "tag_length_aa": null,
      "linker": null,
      "evidence_type": "published tag insertion in the same loop or domain",
      "functional_impact_measured": "yes",
      "confidence": "low",
      "rationale": "Residue K155 lies within the extracellular mucin-like domain (topology O, residues 19-170), 15 residues upstream of the TM boundary (TM starts at 171), well within the >=3-residue safety margin. The sequence context around position 155 (HSEAKK|GSKFDT) represents a transition from the mucin repeat region into a less-glycosylated linker segment (GSKFDTGSFV) connecting to the TM helix, making it more accommodating for an insertion than the dense Ser/Thr O-glycosylation repeats upstream. The SHREK study (PMID 34064525) demonstrated that an HA-tagged TMEM123 (pTMEM123-HA) retains antiviral function, implying the ectodomain tolerates a tag. The mucin-like ectodomain of the related SHREK-family member Vsg (PMID 36171290) also tolerates extracellular insertions in its O-glycosylated mucin-like domain. Position chosen to be >=3 residues from TM and outside the densest glycosylation repeat region. [validation: function_only; position: inferred; source: paper; entailment_verified: True]",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 34064525,
          "citation": "PMID 34064525"
        }
      ],
